    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0157" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/114<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >1/12</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nicholson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-05T15:00:00-06:00">June 5, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Department’s strictly confidential telegram No. 39, June 3, 3 p.m.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d183-f1"/> President Somoza is in full agreement with the
                    principles expressed in the telegram under reference and cordially offers the
                    complete cooperation of the Nicaraguan Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicholson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
